{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.QNavierStokes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.QNavierStokes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:q_viscosity_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"q_viscosity_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L34-L36","doc":"At q = 1, viscosity vanishes (Euler limit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:q_viscosity_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"q_viscosity_pos","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L25-L32","doc":"The q-viscosity is strictly positive for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QNavierStokes.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QNavierStokes.dim","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L23-L23","doc":"Spatial dimension (always 3 for QOU). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QNavierStokes.viscosity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QNavierStokes.viscosity","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L21-L21","doc":"Quantum kinematic viscosity ν_q = (1 − q⁻¹)/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QNavierStokes.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QNavierStokes.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L19-L19","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QNavierStokes.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QNavierStokes.q","kind":"def","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L18-L18","doc":"Substrate parameter q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QNavierStokes.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QNavierStokes.mk","kind":"ctor","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L16-L16","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QNavierStokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QNavierStokes","kind":"structure","line":9,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-navier-stokes.lean#L9-L23","doc":"The **q-deformed Navier-Stokes equation** in categorical form.\n\nThe kinematic viscosity is q-deformed:\n  ν_q = ½(1 − q⁻¹) = ℏ_q/2\n\nFor q > 1, ν_q > 0 provides genuine dissipation.\nAt q = 1, ν_q = 0 recovers the Euler equation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}